Package: arraydesign
Title: Acoustic Receiver Array Design and Track Simulation
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R:
    person("Jacob", "Brownscombe", , "jakebrownscombe@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2496-8764"))
Description: Places acoustic receivers on a depth raster, simulates animal
    tracks as a correlated random walk that stays in water, simulates tag
    transmissions with a random delay along the tracks, and simulates their
    detection by the array. Detection probabilities come from the
    detection-efficiency fields of 'detfield', so the simulated transmissions
    are heard under the model that will analyse the data the array collects.
    Scores a candidate array by positioning the simulated animals with
    'detfield' and comparing the location surfaces with the true positions,
    and reports the share of the water the array covers.
